# React & Vite (AquaFlow)

Stack: Vite, React 19, TypeScript, React Router. Path alias `@/` → `src/` when configured.

## Structure

- `src/app/` — shell, router, icons
- `src/features/` — one folder per page/domain screen
- `src/domain/` — types and pure business helpers
- `src/store/` — context + localStorage persistence
- `src/components/` — shared UI primitives
- `src/styles/` — design tokens and layout CSS

## Components

- Functional components only. Explicit prop types.
- Keep pages thin; put mutations and formulas in domain/store.
- Colocate feature-only UI under `src/features/<name>/`.

```tsx
// ❌ Untyped props
function Card(props) { return <div>{props.title}</div> }

// ✅ Explicit props
type CardProps = { title: string };
function Card({ title }: CardProps) { return <div>{title}</div> }
```

## Styling

- Reuse CSS variables from `src/styles/tokens.css`. Do not invent a new palette.
- Prefer existing class names (`btn`, `card`, `tbl`) over one-off inline styles.
